{"title":"Rill Snacks","sub":"Launching an organic snack brand in UAE supermarkets","type":"Market entry","industry":"Consumer packaged goods","geo":"United Arab Emirates","diff":2,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Price waterfall · retail economics · break-even velocity","prompt":"Rill makes organic baked lentil snacks in Jordan. A UAE distributor can place it in 120 premium supermarkets in Dubai and Abu Dhabi, at a shelf price of $4.00 a pack. The founder wants to know how much Rill would actually earn per pack, and whether the launch can make money.","clarify":[{"q":"Who takes a cut?","a":"VAT is 5% (included in the shelf price). The retailer keeps 30% of the price before VAT; the distributor keeps 15% of what's left."},{"q":"Rill's costs?","a":"$1.12 per pack including production, freight and import duty."},{"q":"Launch costs?","a":"About $270k in year one (listing fees and in-store sampling), then about $110k a year."},{"q":"Benchmark?","a":"Similar premium snacks sell about 20 packs per store per week."}],"structure":{"root":"Can Rill make money in the UAE?","branches":[{"head":"Price waterfall","items":["Shelf price","VAT","Retailer margin","Distributor margin","Rill's net price"]},{"head":"Unit economics","items":["Net price minus cost per pack"]},{"head":"Volume","items":["Packs per store per week","Number of stores"]},{"head":"Launch costs","items":["Listing fees","Sampling and marketing"]}]},"hypothesis":"A lot of the $4.00 goes to VAT, the retailer and the distributor; I'd expect Rill to keep about half. Whether that's enough depends on how fast packs sell in each store.","questions":[{"q":"Walk down from the $4.00 shelf price to what Rill receives per pack, and its margin.","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"388.46pt\" height=\"195.16pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 388.46 195.16\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; str