138eb8\"><rect x=\"35.3\" y=\"10.472\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"149.688\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Where the $4.00 goes ($ per pack)","note":null},"answer":"<ul><li>Remove VAT: $4.00 ÷ 1.05 = $3.81</li><li>Retailer keeps 30%: $2.67 left</li> <li>Distributor keeps 15%: <b>$2.27</b> to Rill (57% of the shelf price)</li> <li>Minus $1.12 cost: <b>$1.15 contribution per pack</b></li></ul>"},{"q":"How many packs per store per week does Rill need to break even in year one and from year two? Compare with the benchmark of 20.","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Year one: $270k ÷ $1.15 ÷ 120 stores ÷ 52 = <b>37.7 packs per store per week</b>.</p> <p>From year two: $110k ÷ $1.15 ÷ 120 ÷ 52 = <b>15.4</b>.</p> <p>At the benchmark of 20: year one −$0.13M, year two +$0.03M.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> expect a loss in year one, then a modest profit if Rill sells like its peers. The year-one loss takes about four more years of benchmark sales to earn back (cumulative break-even in year five), so Rill needs to beat the benchmark.</p>"},{"q":"How would you make the launch work?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Start with fewer stores</b> (the 40 best) to cut listing fees and focus sampling</li> <li><b>Negotiate listing fees</b> against volume, or pay them in instalments</li> <li><b>Sampling and eye-level shelf space</b> in the first three months: trial drives repeat</li> <li><b>Track packs per store per week</b> monthly; agree with the distributor what happens below 10</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Launch, but plan for a year-one loss. Rill keeps $2.27 of the $4.00 shelf price and earns $1.15 per pack; it needs about 38 packs per store per week to break even in year one but only about 15 after that, against a benchmark of 20. At the benchmark, it loses about $127k in year one and earns about $33k a year after. I recommend starting in the best 40 stores, focusing sampling there, and expanding once sales pass the benchmark. Risk: slow sales in year one lead retailers to delist. Next step: agree store-level targets with the distributor.","great":["Walks the price waterfall step by step, including VAT","Converts break-even into packs per store per week","Separates one-off launch costs from ongoing ones","Recommends a staged launch"],"id":40,"slug":"rill-snacks"}